@startuml j4-ask-for-a-person
!include style.iuml
title J4 Asking for a person
actor Patient
participant "Patient chat\n(index.html, chat.js, sync.js)" as Chat
participant "Rules engine\n(core.js)" as Core
database "Browser storage" as LS
participant "api/tickets.js" as Tix
database "Store (Postgres)\nthrough api/_store.js" as Store
participant "Staff page\n(staff/staff.js, staff/tools.js)" as SP
actor Staff
autonumber

Patient -> Chat : taps "Talk to a person", or types "Can I speak to a human?"
Chat -> Core : FD.answer(message, clinic file, language)
Core -> Core : looks in the clinic file first; it has no answer,\nor only the contact line
Core --> Chat : the person reply, status "needs human"
Chat -> Core : FD.addTicket (question, reply, call back)
Core -> LS : the ticket joins this browser's tickets
Chat --> Patient : "I am not sure I can settle this myself, so I have passed your request to our team ...";\nbelow it the call-back form
Chat -> Tix : sync.js: POST /api/tickets (the ticket, with this browser's key)
Tix -> Store : a row in the table tickets
Staff -> SP : on /staff chooses the type "Asked for a person"
SP --> Staff : the ticket, marked "Needs human" and listed under "To call back"
@enduml
